                        "entry_id": "29761095-8d8b-3df6-babb-ec18582018b0",
                        "glosses": [
                            "In Roman Catholicism, the inferior veneration accorded to saints and angels."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "uncountable",
                            "usually"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1d8ebf60-14e1-42c2-b459-78c8aa9fd8fb",
                                "sense_id": "8d48c27f-01ff-38e8-949e-b426b602c7e8",
                                "text": "But paſſing by this fopperie, FIRST the diſtinction of religious worſhip into Latreia and Douleia is denyed, because there is no ſuch thing."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "738cd8f5-7a33-4cb3-9336-529d54ed1e5c",
                                "sense_id": "8d48c27f-01ff-38e8-949e-b426b602c7e8",
                                "text": "But when we kiss the statue of St. Peter, with the intention of honouring St. Peter, this act is only Douleia, because St. Peter himself being only a man is not entitled to Latreia."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7fbc781c-2a22-4d7f-8b0d-ab8652f8a2e5",
                                "sense_id": "8d48c27f-01ff-38e8-949e-b426b602c7e8",
                                "text": "The lowest degree of worship is called douleia (δουλεία) which, they say, is offered to saints and angels."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
